      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2016 International Society of Nephrology. Published by Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Obesity has been associated with chronic kidney disease in adult studies, but little data exist in pediatrics. Nehus et al. offer the first study to show that bariatric surgery in severely obese adolescents is associated with improved renal outcomes. Despite limitations, this study provided compelling evidence that aggressive weight loss intervention can improve renal outcomes in young, severely obese subjects. Further investigation is required to determine mechanisms by which this may occur."
      },
